From: Project Cascadia <noreply@cascadia>
Subject: [PATCH] m1n1: identify all Apple SIO map-range slots

AppleSmartIO2 uses a fixed four-slot map-range table.  The first three
keys were unknown when m1n1's SIO handoff was implemented for Macs, but
the iPad11,6 ADT includes the first slot and therefore rejects the old
placeholder table.

The AppleSmartIO2 135.0.0 binary from iPadOS 17.1.1 contains the exact
key table MINI, APOA, GPOA, MISC.  Name those slots so T8020's MINI and
MISC ranges are copied into the same 64-byte firmware parameter layout
used by Apple's driver.  Missing slots remain zero-filled.

diff --git a/src/sio.c b/src/sio.c
index 5681666..bb4b83f 100644
--- a/src/sio.c
+++ b/src/sio.c
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@ struct copy_rule copy_rules[] = {
         .fw_param = PARAM_MAP_RANGE,
         .blobsize = 16,
         .keyed = true,
-        .keys = {SPACER, SPACER, SPACER, "MISC", NULL},
+        .keys = {"MINI", "APOA", "GPOA", "MISC", NULL},
     },
     {
         .prop = "dmashim",
